\chapter{Thirty portable libraries}
The expanded library is written in MuLL. Both hosts load the same package files,
and callbacks, loops, and allocations participate in the interpreter's existing
budgets. The native \api{math}, \api{text}, and \api{list} services remain
available through the aggregate installer. Package dependencies use the ordinary
isolated loader and per-runtime cache.

\section{Composition and collections}
\api{option} represents presence separately from a nil value; \api{result}
represents success separately from failure. \api{function} provides composition,
partial application, flipping, and iteration. \api{predicate} combines
predicates with short-circuit evaluation and quantifies lists. \api{pair}
constructs and maps two-element lists.

\api{sequence} provides zip, enumeration, one-level flattening, and reversal.
\api{slice} implements checked half-open slices and chunking. \api{search}
finds values and predicates; a found nil is distinguished by an explicit flag.
\api{sort} offers stable comparator-driven insertion sort. \api{set} preserves
first-occurrence order with structural equality. \api{stack}, \api{queue}, and
\api{deque} return new collections, with removals returning a value/rest record.

\begin{mullcode}
val O <- G:LoadLib("option") or G:DieWith("$E?");
val Q <- G:LoadLib("queue") or G:DieWith("$E?");
val q <- Q:Enqueue(Q:Enqueue(Q:New(), O:Some(nil)), O:None());
val first <- Q:Dequeue(q);
G:Assert(first:value:present);
G:Assert(O:GetOr(first:value, 99) == nil);
G:Assert(G:Len(first:rest) == 1);
\end{mullcode}

\section{Numerical building blocks}
\api{vector} supplies dot products, scaling, addition, norms, and normalization.
\api{matrix} checks rectangular shape and implements transpose/multiplication.
\api{statistics} supplies sum, mean, median, and population variance.
\api{integer} checks exact-integer range and supplies gcd, lcm, and floor divmod.
\api{bit} performs unsigned 32-bit logical operations and shifts using exact
binary64 arithmetic. \api{combinatorics} implements bounded factorial/binomial
coefficients and Cartesian products. \api{range} supplies signed-step integer
ranges, half-open membership, and clamping.

\section{Text and interchange}
\api{string} adds byte slices, trimming, prefixes/suffixes, and repetition;
\api{ascii} supplies character predicates and decimal digit conversion.
\api{csv} reads quoted comma-separated fields, doubled quotes, embedded newlines,
and CRLF records, and writes fully quoted LF records. \api{path} normalizes
POSIX lexical paths without filesystem access. \api{url} percent-codes printable
ASCII and tab/CR/LF; plus is literal and arbitrary binary/Unicode escapes are
outside its contract. \api{semver} handles strict three-component core versions,
rejecting prerelease/build suffixes and leading zeros.

\section{Application utilities}
\api{units} converts angles, temperatures, lengths, and time scales.
\api{geometry} implements points and half-open rectangles, distance, area, and
intersection. \api{color} validates byte RGB channels, formats hexadecimal
colors, blends with nearest-integer rounding, and inverts. \api{assert} supplies
named checks, structural equality, inequality, and absolute-tolerance comparison.

\begin{mullcode}
val Csv <- G:LoadLib("csv") or G:DieWith("$E?");
val Stats <- G:LoadLib("statistics") or G:DieWith("$E?");
val A <- G:LoadLib("assert") or G:DieWith("$E?");
val rows <- [["name", "comment"], ["MuLL", "a,b and \"quotes\""]];
A:Equal(Csv:Decode(Csv:Encode(rows)), rows);
A:Equal(Stats:Median([4, 1, 3, 2]), 2.5);
\end{mullcode}
The API catalogue in \api{mull/stdlib/README.md} specifies signatures, failure
cases, and bounds. The shared conformance suite exercises all thirty packages
with optimization enabled and disabled in each host.
